      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T15:54:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about having this be part of the textureAndSampler binding group for now? That would keep it consistent with the dstCopy texture. Both of these are \"intrinsic\" and ought to be bound only once, but we\u0027re still stuck in a suboptimal binding configuration right now. But having the backends treat the storage texture in the same code paths as the dst copy will hopefully make updating to a different binding organization in the future a bit smoother.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 442,
        "startChar": 72,
        "endLine": 442,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "0e44251cfcca63ce49cd60949f9c92c95f894793",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14905dea_732ed789",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ShaderInfo.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-02T22:10:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it should remain on Uniform:\n\n1) By assigning it to the uniform set, the shader layout binding is identical whether the device supports storage buffers or falls back to texture. Neither ShaderInfo nor the backend pipeline layouts need to branch on separate binding layouts for the storage data.\n\n2) The texture sampler bindings depend on the paint; to get a consistent index we would have to make a system where it takes up the 0th index slot or something like that.",
      "parentUuid": "88dc3241_ecacdaf4",
      "range": {
