      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T15:54:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should have realized this when we added the `getDefaultReadableTextureInfo` function, but we don\u0027t need to have these coupled to an SkColorType, since that implies a possible view swizzle and other color conversion operations.  Here, we really do just want data, so we could update `getDefaultReadableTextureInfo` to accept a TextureFormat value.  This would also let us possible switch from kRGBA32F to kR32F if having it be a scalar value makes things easier (but maybe a rgba32f return type is better since it\u0027ll cover loading a float4 in a single sample call).",
      "range": {
