      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T15:54:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine for now, but it is highlighting a gap in functionality with Graphite\u0027s upload functionality. If we are actually wanting to move pure data to a texture, we don\u0027t have any uploadSource path that takes in the texture format bytes directly (although technically, that is what the MakeCompressed() function is doing).\n\nAdditionally, it would be really nice in this case where we have disjoint sources of data to be able to copy them directly to the transfer buffer\u0027s mapped GPU memory to avoid an extra memcpy/allocation.  I an imagine a version of UploadSource that takes in a callback function that gets invoked per row and is provided a BufferWriter (or actually lets us use TextureUploadWriter as a writer instead of a cumbersome 2D copier that it currently is).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 210,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0e44251cfcca63ce49cd60949f9c92c95f894793",
